cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this research software, please cite it using these metadata."

title: "Clinical Readmission Prediction with XGBoost"
type: software
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-08-15"

authors:
  - name: "malahatmrd"

abstract: >-
  A leakage-aware and reproducible clinical machine-learning pipeline for
  predicting 30-day hospital readmission using the Diabetes 130-US Hospitals
  dataset. The project includes patient-independent cohort construction,
  XGBoost optimization, probability calibration, validation-only threshold
  selection, SHAP explainability, subgroup and repeated-encounter robustness
  analyses, and a final locked Test evaluation with bootstrap uncertainty.

repository-code: "https://github.com/malahatmrd/clinical-readmission-xgboost"

license: MIT

keywords:
  - clinical machine learning
  - medical AI
  - readmission prediction
  - XGBoost
  - probability calibration
  - explainable AI
  - SHAP
  - reproducible research
